<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Vedrosha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1500">1500</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscovite-lithuanian-wars">Muscovite–Lithuanian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Vedrosha was fought on 14 July 1500 on the Vedrosha River near Dorogobuzh in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. The Muscovite army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a> defeated the Lithuanian army of Grand Duke Alexander, and its commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstanty-ostrogski">Konstanty Ostrogski</a> was captured. The defeat allowed Muscovy to keep the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/severia">Seversk lands</a> on the upper Oka and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desna-river">Desna</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-vedrosha.jpg" alt="Battle of Vedrosha" width="320" height="348" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andr marc · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Russo%E2%80%93Lithuanian_Wars-1500_campaign-rus0.2.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
